Q: he blushed (passé simple)
A: {{il rougit}}
N: `rougir`; same spelling as the present

---

Q: that he were (imperfect subjunctive)
A: {{qu'il fût}}
N: `être`; the circumflex separates it from `il fut`

---

Q: that he had (imperfect subjunctive)
A: {{qu'il eût}}
N: `avoir`

---

Q: that he saw (imperfect subjunctive)
A: {{qu'il vît}}
N: `voir`

---

Q: that they ate (imperfect subjunctive)
A: {{qu'ils mangeassent}}
N: from Le Petit Prince; modern French: `qu'ils mangent`

---

C: Passé simple, third person: `chanter` → `il [chanta]`, `choisir` → `il [choisit]`, `courir` → `il [courut]`, `retenir` → `il [retint]`.
N: `-a` for `-er` verbs, `-it` for most `-ir` and `-re`, `-ut` for many `-oir`, `-int` for the `venir` and `tenir` family.

---

Q: suddenly
A: {{soudain}}
